<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Basics of dLLMs</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide a more self-contained overview of masked dLLMs. Please also refer to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al. (2024)</a></cite> for more details.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We denote scalars by lowercase letters (<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>), vectors by bold lowercase (<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math>), and sequences by <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{x}_{1:n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1:n}</annotation></semantics></math>. A superscript (e.g., <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math>) denotes an item’s index within a group. We define the set of the first <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> integers as <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[k]\vcentcolon=\{1,\dots,k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[k]\vcentcolon=\{1,\dots,k\}</annotation></semantics></math> and the <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional probability simplex as <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Distributions include the categorical <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{Cat}(\cdot\mid\bm{p})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Cat}(\cdot\mid\bm{p})</annotation></semantics></math> and the uniform <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math>. Throughout the paper, we use the following primary indices: <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math> for position, <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[g]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[g]</annotation></semantics></math> for a sequence in a group, and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> for the continuous diffusion timestep.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We start from a discrete time version of the diffusion models with finite <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume a one-hot categorical variable <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}\in\{e_{1},\dots,e_{k}\}\subset\Delta^{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}\in\{e_{1},\dots,e_{k}\}\subset\Delta^{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Further assume we gradually corrupt <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math> into an absorbing state <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{m}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{[\texttt{mask}]~}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">mask</mtext><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{[\texttt{mask}]~}</annotation></semantics></math>) with transition matrix <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Then:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{x})=\text{Cat}(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\overline{\bm{Q}_{t}}\bm{x})=\text{Cat}(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\prod_{\tau=1}^{t}\bm{Q}_{\tau}\bm{x})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{x})=\text{Cat}(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\overline{\bm{Q}_{t}}\bm{x})=\text{Cat}(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\prod_{\tau=1}^{t}\bm{Q}_{\tau}\bm{x}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is also a one-hot categorical random variable in <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. In practice, one could choose <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{x})=\text{Cat}(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\alpha_{t}\bm{x}+(1-\alpha_{t})\bm{m})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{x})=\text{Cat}(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\alpha_{t}\bm{x}+(1-\alpha_{t})\bm{m}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}=1,\alpha_{T}=0,\alpha^{\prime}_{t}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}=1,\alpha_{T}=0,\alpha^{\prime}_{t}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Normally, the goal is to construct the lower bound of the evidence (ELBO) and maximize it. For this particular case, consider the discretized Markov chain with <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> latent variables <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{1},\bm{z}_{2},\dots,\bm{z}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{1},\bm{z}_{2},\dots,\bm{z}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{T}=\bm{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{T}=\bm{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{1}=\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{1}=\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math>. We use the shorthand <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{z}=\bm{z}_{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}=\bm{z}_{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math> and write</p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}(\bm{x};\bm{{\bm{\theta}}})&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\log\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{x},\bm{z})}{q(\bm{z}\mid\bm{x})}\bigg]\\
=&amp;\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\underbrace{\log p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{1})}_{=0}+\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\log\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})}{q(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1},\bm{x})}+\underbrace{\log\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{T})}{q(\bm{z}_{T}\mid\bm{x})}}_{=0}\bigg]\\
=&amp;\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t},\bm{z}_{t+1}\sim q}\bigg[\log\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})}{q(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1},\bm{x})}\bigg]\\
=&amp;\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t+1}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{z}_{t+1},\bm{x})}\bigg[\log\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})}{q(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1},\bm{x})}\bigg].\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}(\bm{x};\bm{{\bm{\theta}}})&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\log\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{x},\bm{z})}{q(\bm{z}\mid\bm{x})}\bigg]\\
=&amp;\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\underbrace{\log p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{1})}_{=0}+\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\log\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})}{q(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1},\bm{x})}+\underbrace{\log\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{T})}{q(\bm{z}_{T}\mid\bm{x})}}_{=0}\bigg]\\
=&amp;\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t},\bm{z}_{t+1}\sim q}\bigg[\log\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})}{q(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1},\bm{x})}\bigg]\\
=&amp;\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t+1}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{z}_{t+1},\bm{x})}\bigg[\log\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})}{q(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1},\bm{x})}\bigg].\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{x},\bm{z}_{1})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{x},\bm{z}_{1})=0</annotation></semantics></math> because we assume <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{1}=\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{1}=\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{T})=q(\bm{z}_{T}\mid\bm{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{T})=q(\bm{z}_{T}\mid\bm{x})</annotation></semantics></math> because we assume <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{T}=\bm{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{T}=\bm{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. A common method to parameterize <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is via predicting <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math> with model <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\bm{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\bm{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})=q\left(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1},\bm{x}=\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(\cdot\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})=q\left(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1},\bm{x}=\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(\cdot\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now, given that <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is either <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{m}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math> (assuming <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{m}\neq\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒎</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{m}\neq\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math>). Then the KL term in equation <a href="#A1.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Notation. ‣ Appendix A Basics of dLLMs ‣ SPG: Sandwiched Policy Gradient for Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> decomposes into the following.</p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\log\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})}{q(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1},\bm{x})}=\begin{cases}0&amp;\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{x},\\
0&amp;\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{m},\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{x},\qquad{\small{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\text{(Impossible)}}}\\
\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})&amp;\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{x},\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{m},\\
0&amp;\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{m}.\\
\end{cases}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">(Impossible)</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\log\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})}{q(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1},\bm{x})}=\begin{cases}0&amp;\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{x},\\
0&amp;\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{m},\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{x},\qquad{\small{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\text{(Impossible)}}}\\
\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})&amp;\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{x},\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{m},\\
0&amp;\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{m}.\\
\end{cases}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Moreover, <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{m},\bm{x})=\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{t+1}}{1-\alpha_{t+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{m},\bm{x})=\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{t+1}}{1-\alpha_{t+1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and note that <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t})=1</annotation></semantics></math>
when <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, so we have:</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}(\bm{x};\bm{{\bm{\theta}}})&amp;=\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t+1}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{t+1}}{1-\alpha_{t+1}}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})\mathbbm{1}(\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{m})\bigg]\\
&amp;=\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t+1}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{t+1}}{1-\alpha_{t+1}}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})\bigg].~~~{\small{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\text{(If $\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{x}$, then $\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})=0$)}}}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="1.157em">.</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">(If </mtext><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">𝒛</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi></mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">, then </mtext><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">𝒛</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}(\bm{x};\bm{{\bm{\theta}}})&amp;=\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t+1}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{t+1}}{1-\alpha_{t+1}}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})\mathbbm{1}(\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{m})\bigg]\\
&amp;=\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t+1}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{t+1}}{1-\alpha_{t+1}}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})\bigg].~~~{\small{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\text{(If $\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{x}$, then $\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})=0$)}}}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Taking the above limit as <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}(\bm{x};\bm{{\bm{\theta}}})=\int_{t=0}^{1}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}-1}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t})\bigg]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}(\bm{x};\bm{{\bm{\theta}}})=\int_{t=0}^{1}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\frac{\alpha^{\prime}_{t}}{\alpha_{t}-1}\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t})\bigg].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Generalization to Sequence</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The above is for a single categorical variable <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math>. In practice as in language modeling, it becomes a sequence of categorical variables <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{x}_{1:n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1:n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we write</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}(\bm{x}_{1:n};\bm{{\bm{\theta}}})&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{1:n}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x}_{1:n})}\bigg[\log\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{x}_{1:n},\bm{z}_{1:n})}{q(\bm{z}_{1:n}\mid\bm{x}_{1:n})}\bigg]\\
&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{\{\bm{z}_{i}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x}_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}}\bigg[\sum_{i=1}^{n}\log\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{x}_{i},\bm{z}_{1:n})}{q(\bm{z}_{i}\mid\bm{x}_{i})}\bigg]\qquad{\small{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\text{(Independence of $q(\cdot\mid\bm{x}_{i})$)}}}\\
&amp;=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{\{\bm{z}_{i^{\prime}}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x}_{i^{\prime}})\}_{i^{\prime}=1}^{n}}\bigg[\log\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{x}_{i},\bm{z}_{1:n})}{q(\bm{z}_{i}\mid\bm{x}_{i})}\bigg]\\
&amp;=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}(\bm{x}_{i};\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}).\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">(Independence of </mtext><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF00FF;" mathcolor="#FF00FF" mathsize="0.900em">)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}(\bm{x}_{1:n};\bm{{\bm{\theta}}})&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{1:n}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x}_{1:n})}\bigg[\log\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{x}_{1:n},\bm{z}_{1:n})}{q(\bm{z}_{1:n}\mid\bm{x}_{1:n})}\bigg]\\
&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{\{\bm{z}_{i}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x}_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}}\bigg[\sum_{i=1}^{n}\log\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{x}_{i},\bm{z}_{1:n})}{q(\bm{z}_{i}\mid\bm{x}_{i})}\bigg]\qquad{\small{\color[rgb]{1,0,1}\text{(Independence of $q(\cdot\mid\bm{x}_{i})$)}}}\\
&amp;=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{\{\bm{z}_{i^{\prime}}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x}_{i^{\prime}})\}_{i^{\prime}=1}^{n}}\bigg[\log\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{x}_{i},\bm{z}_{1:n})}{q(\bm{z}_{i}\mid\bm{x}_{i})}\bigg]\\
&amp;=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}}(\bm{x}_{i};\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The key distinction from the single-token formulation (mentioned beforehand) is that the reverse process <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is conditioned on all <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{z}_{1:n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{1:n}</annotation></semantics></math> instead of a single token’s <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Evidence Upper Bound for dLLMs</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the derivation of the evidence upper bound. Following the above section, we start from the discrete time version of the diffusion models.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Rényi Variational Bound; <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rényi (1961)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Van Erven and Harremos (2014)</a></cite>)<span id="Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix an observation <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q(\cdot\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\cdot\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> be any distribution on <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(\cdot\mid x)\ll q(\cdot\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≪</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot\mid x)\ll q(\cdot\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math>, denoting that <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(\cdot\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> is absolutely continuous with respect to <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q(\cdot\mid z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\cdot\mid z)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, the following holds for any <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{z\sim q(\cdot\mid x)}\left[\log\frac{p(x,z)}{q(z\mid x)}\right]\leq\log p(x)\leq\frac{1}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}_{z\sim q(\cdot\mid x)}\left[\bigg(\frac{p(x,z)}{q(z\mid x)}\bigg)^{\beta}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{z\sim q(\cdot\mid x)}\left[\log\frac{p(x,z)}{q(z\mid x)}\right]\leq\log p(x)\leq\frac{1}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}_{z\sim q(\cdot\mid x)}\left[\bigg(\frac{p(x,z)}{q(z\mid x)}\bigg)^{\beta}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In view of the above lemma, we derive an evidence upper bound for masked diffusion models in the following theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Evidence Upper Bound for Masked Diffusion)<span id="Thmtheorem1a.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume the forward denoising process has <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> steps with a monotonic schedule <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and a sequence of categorical variables <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{x}_{1:n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{1:n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log\pi_{{\bm{\theta}}}(\bm{x}_{1:n})\leq\mathcal{L}_{\text{EUBO}}(\bm{x}_{1:n};\bm{{\bm{\theta}}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">EUBO</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\pi_{{\bm{\theta}}}(\bm{x}_{1:n})\leq\mathcal{L}_{\text{EUBO}}(\bm{x}_{1:n};\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{EUBO}}(\bm{x}_{1:n};\bm{{\bm{\theta}}})\vcentcolon=\frac{1}{\beta}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\log\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t+1}}\Bigg[\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{t+1}}{1-\alpha_{t+1}}\cdot\mathbbm{1}(\bm{z}_{t+1,i}=\bm{m})\cdot\pi_{{\bm{\theta}}}^{\beta}(\bm{x}_{i}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})\Bigg]+C(T)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">EUBO</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mi>log</mi><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{EUBO}}(\bm{x}_{1:n};\bm{{\bm{\theta}}})\vcentcolon=\frac{1}{\beta}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\log\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t+1}}\Bigg[\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{t+1}}{1-\alpha_{t+1}}\cdot\mathbbm{1}(\bm{z}_{t+1,i}=\bm{m})\cdot\pi_{{\bm{\theta}}}^{\beta}(\bm{x}_{i}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})\Bigg]+C(T),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1a.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1a.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C(T)=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{1:T}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\Big[q(\bm{z}_{1:T}\mid\bm{x})^{-n}\Big],&amp;1\leq\beta&lt;n\\
0,&amp;\beta\geq n\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(T)=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{1:T}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\Big[q(\bm{z}_{1:T}\mid\bm{x})^{-n}\Big],&amp;1\leq\beta&lt;n\\
0,&amp;\beta\geq n\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant independent of <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝛉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first consider the case with a single categorical variable <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math>. On the account of Lemma <a href="#A2.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Lemma 1 (Rényi Variational Bound; ( ) ). ‣ Appendix B Evidence Upper Bound for dLLMs ‣ SPG: Sandwiched Policy Gradient for Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> and following a similar argument as in equation <a href="#A1.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Notation. ‣ Appendix A Basics of dLLMs ‣ SPG: Sandwiched Policy Gradient for Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, for any <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we can write</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(\bm{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\pi_{\bm{\theta}}(\bm{x})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\left[\bigg(\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{x},\bm{z})}{q(\bm{z}\mid\bm{x})}\bigg)^{\beta}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\left[\bigg(\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{x},\bm{z})}{q(\bm{z}\mid\bm{x})}\bigg)^{\beta}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad=\frac{1}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{1:T}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\prod_{t=1}^{T-1}\bigg(\frac{p_{\bm{\theta}}(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})}{q(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1},\bm{x})}\bigg)^{\beta}\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad=\frac{1}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{1:T}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\prod_{t=1}^{T-1}\bigg(\frac{p_{\bm{\theta}}(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})}{q(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1},\bm{x})}\bigg)^{\beta}\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Note that the sequence <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{z}_{1:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}_{1:T}</annotation></semantics></math> has a form <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bm{x},\dots,\bm{x},\bm{m},\dots,\bm{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒎</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bm{x},\dots,\bm{x},\bm{m},\dots,\bm{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the transition event:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{A}_{t}\coloneqq\{\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{x},\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{A}_{t}\coloneqq\{\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{x},\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then, by the law of total expectations, equation <a href="#A2.E18" title="Equation 18 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B Evidence Upper Bound for dLLMs ‣ SPG: Sandwiched Policy Gradient for Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> can be expressed as:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{1:T}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\prod_{t=1}^{T-1}\bigg(\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})}{q(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1},\bm{x})}\bigg)^{\beta}\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{1:T}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\prod_{t=1}^{T-1}\bigg(\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})}{q(\bm{z}_{t}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1},\bm{x})}\bigg)^{\beta}\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{\beta}\log\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{A}_{t})\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\left[\prod_{s=1}^{T-1}\bigg(\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{s}\mid\bm{z}_{s+1})}{q(\bm{z}_{s}\mid\bm{z}_{s+1},\bm{x})}\bigg)^{\beta}\middle|\mathcal{A}_{t}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{\beta}\log\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{A}_{t})\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\left[\prod_{s=1}^{T-1}\bigg(\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{s}\mid\bm{z}_{s+1})}{q(\bm{z}_{s}\mid\bm{z}_{s+1},\bm{x})}\bigg)^{\beta}\middle|\mathcal{A}_{t}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{\beta}\log\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t+1}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\mathbbm{1}(\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{m})q(\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{m},\bm{x})\bigg(\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{m})}{q(\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{m},\bm{x})}\bigg)^{\beta}\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{\beta}\log\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t+1}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\mathbbm{1}(\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{m})q(\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{m},\bm{x})\bigg(\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{m})}{q(\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{m},\bm{x})}\bigg)^{\beta}\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E20.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{\beta}\log\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t+1}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\mathbbm{1}(\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{m})\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{t+1}}{1-\alpha_{t+1}}\pi_{{\bm{\theta}}}^{\beta}(\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{\beta}\log\sum_{t=1}^{T-1}\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{t+1}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\mathbbm{1}(\bm{z}_{t+1}=\bm{m})\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{t+1}}{1-\alpha_{t+1}}\pi_{{\bm{\theta}}}^{\beta}(\bm{x}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">The penultimate line is due to the fact that conditioned on the event <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the ratio <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{s}\mid\bm{z}_{s+1})}{q(\bm{z}_{s}\mid\bm{z}_{s+1},\bm{x})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{s}\mid\bm{z}_{s+1})}{q(\bm{z}_{s}\mid\bm{z}_{s+1},\bm{x})}</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to one for any <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\neq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\neq t</annotation></semantics></math>. The last line uses the formula for <math id="A2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>. The indicator <math id="A2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbbm{1}(\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbbm{1}(\bm{z}_{t}=\bm{m})</annotation></semantics></math> appears in the final expression because the terms in the bound are only non-trivial when the model must make a prediction from a corrupted state.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we generalize the above to a sequence of categorical variables <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{x}=\bm{x}_{1:n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}=\bm{x}_{1:n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similar as <a href="#A2.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Evidence Upper Bound for dLLMs ‣ SPG: Sandwiched Policy Gradient for Masked Diffusion Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\log\pi_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{x}_{1:n})\leq\frac{1}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{1:T}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\prod_{t=1}^{T-1}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bigg(\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{t,i}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})}{q(\bm{z}_{t,i}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1},\bm{x})}\bigg)^{\beta}\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\pi_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{x}_{1:n})\leq\frac{1}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{1:T}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\prod_{t=1}^{T-1}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bigg(\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{t,i}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})}{q(\bm{z}_{t,i}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1},\bm{x})}\bigg)^{\beta}\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Denote <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{C}(T)\vcentcolon=\frac{1}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{1:T}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\Big[q(\bm{z}_{1:T}\mid\bm{x})^{-n}\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{C}(T)\vcentcolon=\frac{1}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{1:T}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\Big[q(\bm{z}_{1:T}\mid\bm{x})^{-n}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math>. The upper bound in the RHS can be further derived as</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{1:T}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\prod_{t=1}^{T-1}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bigg(\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{t,i}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})}{q(\bm{z}_{t,i}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1},\bm{x})}\bigg)^{\beta}\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}_{\bm{z}_{1:T}\sim q(\cdot\mid\bm{x})}\bigg[\prod_{t=1}^{T-1}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\bigg(\frac{p_{\bm{{\bm{\theta}}}}(\bm{z}_{t,i}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1})}{q(\bm{z}_{t,i}\mid\bm{z}_{t+1},\bm{x})}\bigg)^{\beta}\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
